From 1aff0cc9d117acc035385619da5a35593c45ed6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 23:37:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(documenteditor): Layout Options button and object
 anchor like Word

When one picture, shape or chart is selected, a button appears next to
its top right corner and opens Word's Layout Options flyout: In Line
with Text; With Text Wrapping (Square, Tight, Through, Top and Bottom,
Behind Text, In Front of Text) with Word-like icons; Move with text /
Fix position on page; See more... (Layout dialog, Position tab). The
wrapping choices go through the ribbon's Wrap Text menu, so an inline
picture that starts floating keeps its place; "Fix position on page"
and "Move with text" convert the position so that the object does not
move. The anchor of a floating object is drawn in the margin next to
its paragraph, with a lock when the anchor is locked. The button and
the anchor hide while the object is dragged or resized and follow
scrolling and zoom. Keyboard: arrows between the choices, Esc closes.

New module app/elixir-images (controller ElixirImages, view
ElixirLayoutOptions); strings in en, fr, de, es, it, pt, pt-pt, nl, ru,
pl, ja and zh, Word's own terms.

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
